text.section:
If a trust qualifies for a special tax benefit or a fiduciary is not an independent person:

The unitrust rate established under § 64.2-1044 may not be less than three percent or more than five percent;


The only provisions of § 64.2-1045 that apply are subsection A and subdivisions B 1, B 4, B 5 a, and B 9 of § 64.2-1045;


The only period that may be used under § 64.2-1046 is a calendar year under subdivision A 1 of § 64.2-1046; and


The only other provisions of § 64.2-1046 that apply are subdivisions B 2 a and B 3 of § 64.2-1046.
